From: alphx61-claude <taranrajput11@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 22:19:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] backlight: Add TI LMU (LM3632) backlight driver

drivers/mfd/ti-lmu.c registers a "ti-lmu-backlight" cell for the
LM3632, but no driver for that cell was ever merged, so on boards using
this chip the backlight stays off even when the panel initialises
correctly.

Add a driver for it. Brightness is 11 bit, split over the two brightness
registers. The chip is put into I2C brightness mode because the PWM
input is not wired up on all boards, and leaving it in PWM mode there
would keep the backlight dark.

The LDOs generating the +-5.5V panel bias are already handled by
lm363x-regulator, so this only covers the backlight itself.
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WBT8fxGbtA4EKiL94VBvk2
---
 drivers/video/backlight/Kconfig            |   8 +
 drivers/video/backlight/Makefile           |   1 +
 drivers/video/backlight/ti-lmu-backlight.c | 184 +++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 193 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/video/backlight/ti-lmu-backlight.c

diff --git a/drivers/video/backlight/Kconfig b/drivers/video/backlight/Kconfig
index 51387b1ef..1166f1aa5 100644
--- a/drivers/video/backlight/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/video/backlight/Kconfig
@@ -389,6 +389,14 @@ config BACKLIGHT_LM3639
 	help
 	  This supports TI LM3639 Backlight + 1.5A Flash LED Driver
 
+config BACKLIGHT_TI_LMU
+	tristate "Backlight driver for TI LMU (LM3632)"
+	depends on MFD_TI_LMU
+	help
+	  Say Y to enable the backlight driver for the TI LMU LM3632.
+	  The MFD core registers a backlight cell for this chip but no
+	  driver existed for it, so the backlight stayed off.
+
 config BACKLIGHT_LP855X
 	tristate "Backlight driver for TI LP855X"
 	depends on I2C && PWM
